  "earned_statement": "The canonical five-matching S5 quotient determines a unique Aut(G60)-equivariant bijection from its ten unordered duads to the ten inverse pairs of roots of tau. No equivariant bijection exists from the twenty ordered duads to the twenty individual roots. The duad and inverse-pair actions have pointwise kernel Z2(A)=V4, while root conjugation has pointwise kernel Z1(A)=C2. The residual quotient Z2(A)/Z1(A)=C2 exchanges every root with its inverse. Thus the native unoriented graph selects one reversal-covariant pair, not one orientation.",
